# i18n vs localization (Payload)

Follow Payload’s own split — do **not** invent a parallel copy system.

| Concern | Payload API | Docs |
|---------|-------------|------|
| **UI / interface strings** | `i18n` + `t('namespace:key')` | [configuration/i18n](https://payloadcms.com/docs/configuration/i18n) |
| **CMS / database content** | `localization` + `localized: true` + `locale` on queries | [configuration/localization](https://payloadcms.com/docs/configuration/localization) |

## UI strings (i18n)

1. Add keys under the host’s custom translation bundles (typically `custom` in the project’s i18n package or `i18n.translations`).
2. Wire those bundles into `buildConfig({ i18n: { translations } })`.
3. **Resolve strings where they render**, using Payload’s server vs client APIs
   ([docs](https://payloadcms.com/docs/custom-components/overview#getting-the-current-language)):

| Side | Obtain language | Resolve |
|------|-----------------|---------|
| **Server** | `await getRequestI18n()`, `req.i18n`, or the `i18n` prop | `t('custom:…')` / `i18n.t` for dictionary keys; `getTranslation(label, i18n)` from `@payloadcms/translations` for Payload labels |
| **Client** | `useTranslation()` (or the host’s wrapper) | `t('custom:…')` — same keys |

Prefer server resolution when the string is rendered in an RSC (or when pairing with a CMS `locale` query). Do not invent per-page `build*Copy` maps that re-list every key.

When a shared UI package cannot import `@payloadcms/ui`, pass **`t`** (or the whole `i18n`) as a prop.

## Database content (localization)

- Host enables `localization` when needed.
- Mark CMS fields `localized: true`.
- Read/write with `locale` on Local/REST API.
- Do **not** put CMS document strings into the UI i18n dictionary.

## Do not

- Hardcode member-facing English in UI components.
- Invent `build*Copy` helpers that manually map every key.
- Mix UI `t()` keys with DB `localized` field values as if they were the same mechanism.
